    "result_text": "All tests pass across the full suite (exit 0, no failures or errors in any surefire report).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store and compare numbers in E.164 form.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `toE164(String)` helper implementing the normalization rules:\n- Strips spaces, dashes and brackets.\n- If a leading `+` and country code are present, keeps them.\n- Otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`; returns `null` (\u2192 400) otherwise.\n\n`normalizeTelephone` now writes the E.164 string back onto the request (so `'0412 345 678'` \u2192 `'+61412345678'`), and `rejectDuplicateTelephone` normalizes each stored owner's telephone through `toE164` before comparing, so `'0412 345 678'` and `'+61 412 345 678'` collide (409).\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the old `@Digits(integer=10)` / `^[0-9]{10}$` constraints (which would have rejected the `+`-prefixed value on persist) with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`, and dropped the now-unused `@Digits` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` description and example to document the E.164 behaviour.\n\nVerified against the acceptance tests: Cp02 (stores E.164), Cp03 (duplicate compared as E.164 \u2192 409), Cp08 (national\u2192E.164, keeps explicit country code, rejects unformattable `'12'` \u2192 400), and Cp01 (blank telephone still 400), plus the full suite green.",
